      <div type="clause" n="70.20">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 70.20</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 70.20" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="589" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis sine liberis decesserit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.28"/>, pater aut mater eius in hereditatem succedant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.29"/>, uel frater aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.30"/> soror, si pater et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.31"/> mater desint<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.32"/>.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 589 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">589</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dessess. <hi rend="italic">Sc;</hi> disc. <hi rend="italic">Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dessess. Sc; disc. Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">589</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-at <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-at Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">589</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">Wh</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uel Wh</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">589</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so K;</hi> aut <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so K; aut the rest</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">589</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">desinunt <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">desinunt Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_70-20.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Erbgang 23. a; Aszendentenfolge ist nicht im Normann. Rechte und noch bei Glanvilla nicht kraft festen Grundsatzes ausgeschlossen; Brunner <hi rend="italic">Agnorm. Erbfolge</hi> 22; in den Nachlass Kinderloser sukzedieren Aszendenten unter Ausschluss der ihnen erst nachstehenden Geschwister im Schwed. Rechte; Fritz <hi rend="italic">Gesetzl. Verwandt</hi>. in <hi rend="italic">Sav. Zs. RG., Germ</hi>. 36, 149</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Erbgang 23. a; succession by ascendants is not excluded by any fixed principle in Norman law, nor yet in Glanvilla; Brunner <hi rend="italic">Agnorm. Erbfolge</hi> 22; in Swedish law ascendants succeed to the estate of the childless, to the exclusion of the brothers and sisters, who rank only after them; Fritz <hi rend="italic">Gesetzl. Verwandt</hi>. in <hi rend="italic">Sav. Zs. RG., Germ</hi>. 36, 149</seg></note>
      </div>
